    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hegarty Properties are delighted to present No. 31 Sundays Well Avenue, a wonderfully characterful period residence tucked into one of Cork city's most historic and sought-after settings. Dating from 1900, this handsome end-of-terrace townhouse extends over three floors to approximately 113 sq.m (1,218 sq.ft.) and retains a wealth of original features throughout.\r\nFull of warmth and personality, the home offers bright and generously proportioned rooms, including a welcoming front sitting room with feature fireplace, original shutters and high ceilings, and a lovely open-plan kitchen/dining area complete with a charming old stove. Characterful details such as exposed feature beams, decorative fireplaces and traditional shutters add real appeal at every turn, while the flexible layout provides five bedrooms and two bathrooms across the upper floors.\r\nSundays Well is one of Cork's most established and leafy residential neighbourhoods, set on the elevated northern banks of the River Lee and just moments from the heart of the city. Residents enjoy easy access to the city centre, UCC, the Mardyke and Fitzgerald's Park, along with a wonderful choice of schools, shops and local amenities close at hand. A rare opportunity to acquire a home of genuine character in this enduringly popular location.\r\n\r\nAccommodation includes: Entrance Hall, Guest WC, Sitting Room, Open-Plan Kitchen/Dining Room, 5 Bedrooms, 2 Bathrooms and Attic. Circa 1,218 sq.ft.\r\n\r\nGuide Price: €305,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\r\nEntrance Hall:\tWelcoming hall with tiled floor.\r\n\r\nSitting Room:\tBright and inviting reception room with wood floor, feature fireplace, high ceilings, original shutters and lovely period detailing.\r\nKitchen/Dining \r\nRoom:\tA characterful open-plan space. The dining area features a wood floor and a charming old stove, while the fully fitted kitchen offers generous storage and a door to the rear yard. Fridge freezer, washing machine, double oven and grill included.\r\n\r\nGround Floor WC:\tConveniently positioned beneath the stairs, comprising electric shower, WC and wash hand basin.\r\nFirst Floor:\r\nBedroom 1:\tGenerous double bedroom.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2:\tSecond well-proportioned double bedroom.\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom: \tFully appointed bathroom with bath, electric shower, WC and wash hand basin.\r\nSecond Floor:\r\nBedrooms 3, 4 & 5: \tThree further bedrooms, full of character with feature exposed \r\nbeams and original detailing.\r\n\r\nAttic: \tAttic space accessed off the second floor, offering handy storage.\r\n\r\nOutside:  \t\r\nFront: \tAttractive period frontage with characterful rendered façade and arched window detailing addressing the street.\r\nRear: \tEnclosed rear yard accessed directly from the kitchen."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tCharacterful period end-of-terrace residence dating from 1900 \r\n•\tApprox. 113 sq.m. / 1,218 sq.ft. over three floors \r\n•\tFive bedrooms and two bathrooms \r\n•\tWealth of original period features including exposed beams, fireplaces and shutters \r\n•\tBright open-plan kitchen/dining area with characterful old stove \r\n•\tMains gas central heating \r\n•\tMains water and mains sewerage \r\n•\tEnclosed rear yard \r\n•\tHighly sought-after Sundays Well location \r\n•\tWalking distance to Cork City Centre, UCC and a host of local amenities"
